cripts/boardctl validate` -> `RESULT: OK`; `ruff check .` and `ruff format --check .` -> exit 0; GitReins verdict 5bf7e7d7 tier1 PASS + tier2 PASS, commit field 75e94a3 matches the pushed HEAD.\n\nResidual: origin/main advanced twice during the tick (CF-115, CF-116), so the worktree was re-synced to 71e09eb for the GREEN measurement and this board commit advances origin/main once more — re-run the census after it. This repo has no CI workflows (`gh run list` returns []), so ci_result stays SKIP; the gates are `tests/selftest.sh` and the GitReins guard.\n","worktree":"/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/cf114-tick-20261103-2000/repo","branch":"main"}
 {"id":"CF-115","title":"P4 — the CF-099 drift probe certifies two legs it never measures: a milestone with no open-defect list prints OK, and the acceptance plan reverse table is never read","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:03:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:03:56Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"9fa9cfa69257639c4d6c3e00ec68a7510da05228a83f9eade263365d6444106d"},"reasoning":"Measured at 6e8621f from a clean clone of origin/main. Arm A: rewording the PRD milestone phrase \"open defects on this path are\" to \"remaining gaps on this path are\" (a pure prose edit) makes docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exit 0, print \"open_blockers=\" empty and still print OK agree at HEAD, because the open-blocker leg is keyed on sed -n \"s/.*open defects//p\" and an absent phrase makes the loop body vacuous. Arm D: deleting the acceptance plan reverse-direction table row for sections 22-28 (22 table rows to 21) leaves the probe at exit 0 with the same OK line, because the probe never opens that table although AC4 of CF-099 requires an entry for every selftest section. Control arm B: inserting a COMPLETE id into the open-defect list exits 1 with DRIFT naming that id, so the instrument works where it is wired. Distinct from CF-113 (the reverse-mapping CONTENT is false because the section census cannot see lettered sub-arms) and from CF-069 (the selftest board arm is fail-open): this is the probe certifying legs it does not evaluate.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce at the current tree from the repository root: the probe field of this row prints a measured line whose open_blockers= value is empty, then probe_rc=0, on a clone whose PRD milestone phrase was reworded and whose acceptance-plan reverse table lost its sections 22-28 row.\n1. docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exits nonzero and names BOTH legs: a milestone Status block with no open-defect phrase (or an empty list after it) is reported as DRIFT, and any selftest section with no reverse-table row in docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md is reported as DRIFT naming the section.\n2. Re-running the row probe after the fix exits 1 and prints both named DRIFT lines; the control arm (a complete id listed as an open blocker) still exits 1 with its own DRIFT line, so the legs that worked are not weakened.\n3. A committed artifact under docs/audits/ (or a selftest arm) records both arms with their exit codes, regenerated from the fixed tree.\n4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS and bash scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK at the fixed tip.\n5. No PRD requirement or acceptance-plan section is added, removed or weakened: the diff touches docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh plus its evidence artifact or a tests/selftest.sh arm only.","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"probe":"d=$(mktemp -d) && git clone -q . \"$d/repo\" && sed -i \"s/open defects on this path are /remaining gaps on this path are /\" \"$d/repo/docs/PRD-code-factory.md\" && sed -i \"/^| §22–§28 /d\" \"$d/repo/docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md\" && ( cd \"$d/repo\" && out=$(bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh 2>&1); rc=$?; printf \"%s\\n\" \"$out\"; echo \"probe_rc=$rc\" ) && rm -rf \"$d\""}
 {"id":"CF-116","title":"P3 \u2014 the census coverage assertion counts rows, so a mid-run insert mints a duplicate plus a missing row with received == total and the recipe still exits 0","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","reasoning":["Measured 2026-11-03 by the docs-QA lane at 0c765f6 with the committed stand-in docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py, which models a project inserted between the two page fetches: page offset=0 serves rows 0..499 of a 600-row list, then the list shifts by one, so page offset=500 serves row 499 a second time and never serves row 500. BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh prints the count line 600 and 600 row lines and exits 0, while the output holds 599 distinct rows, has no code-factory-p500 line and prints code-factory-p499 twice. CF-089's accepted fix compares received rows against the first reported total (tests/selftest.sh arm 25, fixture mode=short, 'rows received=865 != total reported=866'); that assertion is satisfied exactly by this shape. The row's own trigger class \u2014 a scheduler restart or load-shed between two pages \u2014 also covers an insert between two pages, because offset pagination over a list that mutates mid-run shifts every later offset. Nothing in the tree enumerates identities: the count line comes from wc -l over rows appended blindly with jq -c '.projects[]'. Scheduler project rows carry id=null (GET /api/v1/projects?limit=1), so the identity key is .name."],"acceptance_criteria":["1. Reproduce at the current tree: the probe prints census_rc=0, row_lines=600, distinct_rows=599, p500=MISSING, p499_occurrences=2 \u2014 a complete-looking census that dropped one row and counted another twice. 2. The census asserts identity coverage, not just count: it refuses with a named message and a nonzero exit when an enumerated .name repeats or the distinct count is below the reported total, naming the measured numbers (distinct, duplicates, total) and one concrete duplicated or missing identity. The README.md fence under 'The lanes' and docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh carry the same change and stay textually identical. 3. A tests/selftest.sh arm proves the check can fail: a fixture mode that serves the duplicated boundary row plus the hole prints the named refusal at exit 1 with no census printed, while arms 22-25 still pass unchanged. 4. The live scheduler census still prints 19 rows and exits 0; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS; scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK."],"probe":"(timeout 40 python3 docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py --port 18996 >/dev/null 2>&1 &); sleep 2; BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh >/tmp/cf116-census.out 2>&1; echo \"census_rc=$?\"; echo \"row_lines=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"; echo \"distinct_rows=$(grep '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out | sort -u | wc -l)\"; if grep -q '^code-factory-p500 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out; then echo \"p500=present\"; else echo \"p500=MISSING\"; fi; echo \"p499_occurrences=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p499 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"","detail":{"filed_by":"code-factory-docs-qa-2026-11-03-19-51-49","reproduced_at":"0c765f6"}}
+{"id":"CF-117","title":"P2 — two gate runs at one HEAD red each other: the census fixtures bind literal ports 19022-19029, and a second unexplained arm reddens under concurrency","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:33:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:33:26Z","reasoning":"9. Two simultaneous gate runs at one HEAD red each other. Measured by the code-factory-perf tick code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-20-24-59 at tip 25d1e71 in two fresh clones (never worktrees): serial control SELFTEST: PASS x3 (user+sys 9.37 / 8.31 / 7.69 s, loadavg 11-16); concurrent control run 1 both arms red (A: FAIL (2) auth stats 401 + auth marker; B: FAIL (3) those two plus 'census missing-total guard (exit 99): fixture did not start: ... OSError: [Errno 98] Address already in use'); concurrent run 2 (loadavg 23) A: FAIL (7) all seven census arms, each 'curl: (7) Failed to connect to 127.0.0.1 port 1902x', B: PASS. Cause of that class confirmed in source: cf089_run (tests/selftest.sh:776-801) handed literal ports 19022-19029 to docs/audits/cf089-census-standin.py, so the loser of a bind race either died at startup or read the other run's server mid-arm. FIXED here: the stand-in binds an ephemeral port and publishes it via --port-file, cf089_run reads it inside the existing 50 x 0.05 s readiness budget, and the independent foreman control (two fresh clones, two rounds, loadavg 8.9) now returns a_rc=0 b_rc=0, both SELFTEST: PASS, port_red_lines=0; serial gate unchanged at 7.74 / 8.54 / 9.00 s user+sys and 53 named rows. A SECOND, independent race surfaced in the auth arms and is attributed, not fixed here: scripts/verify-node.sh:42 writes its status body to the fixed path /tmp/node-status.json and line 45 greps that same path, so two concurrent runs exchange bodies (worker receipt: 7 of 12 concurrent arms whose own body carried no auth_required exited 0 after reading the other run's body; reproduced at pre-fix 25d1e71 with verify-node.sh untouched). That defect is owned by CF-072 AC-2 (per-run mktemp body path, removed on exit); it is not attributable to the port class and no assertion was loosened to hide it.","acceptance_criteria":"1. No census arm in tests/selftest.sh (§22-§27) may depend on a fixed TCP port: cf089_run must obtain the port the stand-in actually bound (ephemeral bind) and use it for the readiness poll, the recipe BASE, and cleanup. Quoted evidence: two simultaneous gate runs in two fresh clones at the fixed tree both exit 0 with SELFTEST: PASS and neither output contains 'Address already in use' or 'Failed to connect to 127.0.0.1 port 1902'.\n2. Every assertion is preserved: the gate still prints the same named PASS rows for §22-§27 with the same expected message strings (offset=500 fetch failure, HTTP 502, missing/invalid .projects, rows received=865 != total reported=866, healthy 2-row census, missing total), and §28 (README census mirror agreement) still passes. No arm is deleted, renamed, or loosened, and no timeout is removed.\n3. The stand-in still serves its fixture semantics unchanged (866 rows, 502 at offset=500, two code-factory rows at index 0 and 600) and leaks no server: every cf089_run kills and waits its fixture, and a run leaves no listening socket behind.\n4. Serial gate at the fixed tree is SELFTEST: PASS with rc=0 and a whole-gate user+sys no worse than the pre-fix baseline (9.37 / 8.31 / 7.69 s at loadavg 11-16, same host regime quoted beside the number).\n5. docs/audits/code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-concurrency.md records the before/after concurrent-arm receipt (command, both arms' rc and summary lines, the red row text before, the green text after) and the open auth-arm sub-finding.","detail":{"fingerprint":"4f4615532b8a783c9fcfc9d740850ee269e3a27904ad7e7f6fecee2ace0f7299"},"probe":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Concurrent-gate control: two simultaneous runs of tests/selftest.sh in two fresh clones\n# of this checkout's HEAD. Signature of the defect: a row that FAILs in one arm while\n# PASSing in the other (the loser of a shared-resource race), i.e. unique_red_rows > 0.\n# Post-fix expectation: a_rc=0, b_rc=0, both SELFTEST: PASS, unique_red_rows=0 in both arms.\nset -uo pipefail\nd=$(mktemp -d)\nfor c in 1 2; do git clone -q . \"$d/c$c\" || { echo \"clone $c failed\"; exit 9; }; done\n( cd \"$d/c1\" && bash tests/selftest.sh >\"$d/a.out\" 2>&1; echo $? >\"$d/a.rc\" ) &\n( cd \"$d/c2\" && bash tests/selftest.sh >\"$d/b.out\" 2>&1; echo $? >\"$d/b.rc\" ) &\nwait\nfor arm in a b; do\n  grep '^  FAIL  ' \"$d/$arm.out\" | sed 's/^  FAIL  //' | LC_ALL=C sort -u > \"$d/$arm.f\"\n  grep '^  PASS  ' \"$d/$arm.out\" | sed 's/^  PASS  //' | LC_ALL=C sort -u > \"$d/$arm.p\"\ndone\nfor arm in a b; do\n  LC_ALL=C comm -23 \"$d/$arm.f\" \"$d/$( [ \"$arm\" = a ] && echo b || echo a ).f\" > \"$d/$arm.u\"\n  printf '%s_rc=%s %s_summary=%s unique_red_rows=%s\\n' \"$arm\" \"$(cat \"$d/$arm.rc\")\" \"$arm\" \\\n    \"$(grep '^SELFTEST:' \"$d/$arm.out\")\" \"$(wc -l < \"$d/$arm.u\")\"\n  sed 's/^/    /' \"$d/$arm.u\"\ndone\nprintf 'port_red_lines=%s\\n' \"$(cat \"$d/a.out\" \"$d/b.out\" | grep -c 'Address already in use\\|Failed to connect to 127.0.0.1 port 190')\"\nprintf 'loadavg=%s\\n' \"$(cat /proc/loadavg)\"\nrm -rf \"$d\""}
